WEBVTT

00:00:04.600 --> 00:00:07.040
Okay, let's get this over with.

00:00:07.520 --> 00:00:09.520
"Three little kittens
loved to play,

00:00:09.560 --> 00:00:11.600
they had fun in the sun all day.

00:00:11.680 --> 00:00:13.760
"Then their mother came out
and said,

00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:15.880
'Time for kittens to go to bed."'

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:19.720
Wow! This is garbage.
You actually like this?

00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:21.200
Keep reading!

00:00:21.960 --> 00:00:24.240
- Come on!
- All right, all right, all right.

00:00:24.320 --> 00:00:26.800
"Three little kittens
started to bawl,

00:00:26.880 --> 00:00:29.120
"'Mommy, we're not tired at all.'

00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:31.640
"Their mother smiled
and said with a purr,

00:00:31.720 --> 00:00:35.240
"'Fine, but at least
you should brush your fur."'

00:00:35.320 --> 00:00:37.400
Now you brush the fur.

00:00:39.040 --> 00:00:40.720
This is literature?

00:00:40.800 --> 00:00:43.880
A 2-year-old could have written
this. All right.

00:00:44.440 --> 00:00:47.320
"Three little kittens
with fur all brushed

00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:50.680
"said, 'We can't sleep,
we feel too rushed! '

00:00:50.760 --> 00:00:53.720
"Their mother replied,
with a voice like silk,

00:00:53.800 --> 00:00:56.600
"'Fine, but at least
you should drink your milk."'

00:00:56.680 --> 00:00:58.880
Now make them drink the milk.

00:01:03.080 --> 00:01:06.800
I don't like this book.
This is going on forever.

00:01:06.880 --> 00:01:09.880
"Three little kittens,
with milk all gone,

00:01:09.920 --> 00:01:12.960
rubbed their eyes
and started to yawn.

00:01:19.080 --> 00:01:21.840
"'We can't sleep,
we can't even try.'

00:01:21.880 --> 00:01:24.640
Then their mother sang a lullaby.

00:01:24.720 --> 00:01:27.440
"'Good night kittens,
close your eyes.

00:01:27.480 --> 00:01:30.240
Sleep in peace until you rise.

00:01:30.800 --> 00:01:33.880
"'Though while you sleep,
we are apart,

00:01:33.960 --> 00:01:38.520
"'your mommy loves you
with all her heart."'

00:01:42.360 --> 00:01:44.600
The end. Okay, good night.

00:01:45.560 --> 00:01:47.720
- Wait!
- What?

00:01:47.800 --> 00:01:49.600
What about good night kisses?

00:01:51.480 --> 00:01:55.080
No, no. There will be no kissing
or hugging or kissing.

00:01:57.880 --> 00:02:00.360
He is not gonna kiss us good night,
Agnes.

00:02:00.960 --> 00:02:02.880
I like him. He's nice.

00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:04.280
But scary.

00:02:05.480 --> 00:02:06.720
Like Santa!

00:02:24.480 --> 00:02:28.520
Only 48 hours till the launch,
and all systems are go.

00:02:30.680 --> 00:02:32.280
About that,

00:02:32.760 --> 00:02:36.840
I was thinking that maybe
we could move the date of the
heist.

00:02:36.920 --> 00:02:39.560
Please tell me this is not
as a result

00:02:39.600 --> 00:02:42.280
of the girls' dance recital, is it?

00:02:42.360 --> 00:02:44.480
No, no, no!

00:02:44.560 --> 00:02:47.480
The recital? Don't...
That's stupid!

00:02:47.600 --> 00:02:52.280
I just think it's kind of weird
to do it on a Saturday.

00:02:52.360 --> 00:02:57.720
I was thinking, maybe a heist
is a Tuesday thing, right?

00:02:58.400 --> 00:03:01.880
Gru, you and I have been
working on this for years.

00:03:01.960 --> 00:03:03.960
It's everything we've dreamed of.

00:03:04.040 --> 00:03:05.880
Your chance to make history,

00:03:05.960 --> 00:03:09.040
become the man who stole the moon!

00:03:09.120 --> 00:03:12.760
But these girls
are becoming a major distraction!

00:03:12.840 --> 00:03:14.120
They need to go.

00:03:14.840 --> 00:03:18.680
If you don't do something about it,
then I will.

00:03:20.280 --> 00:03:21.880
I understand.

00:03:24.280 --> 00:03:25.720
Good.

00:03:28.720 --> 00:03:29.840
Butt.

00:03:32.920 --> 00:03:34.080
Butt.

00:03:46.120 --> 00:03:47.240
Butt.

00:03:49.040 --> 00:03:52.640
All right.
Now, when we put our cups together,

00:03:52.720 --> 00:03:55.280
we will make the "clink" sound
with our mouths.

00:03:55.360 --> 00:03:56.480
Ready? Edith?

00:03:56.560 --> 00:03:57.560
- Clink.
- Clink.

00:03:57.640 --> 00:03:59.560
There we go. And now we drink.

00:04:00.280 --> 00:04:01.280
And Agnes?

00:04:01.360 --> 00:04:02.400
- Clink.
- Clink.

00:04:02.480 --> 00:04:03.800
Very good!

00:04:05.440 --> 00:04:06.760
Excuse me, girls.

00:04:07.120 --> 00:04:08.200
Come on!

00:04:08.280 --> 00:04:11.680
Don't worry, I'll be back.
Keep clinking.

00:04:12.120 --> 00:04:13.200
- Clink, clink.
- Clink, clink.

00:04:15.480 --> 00:04:17.280
Miss Hattie,
what are you doing here?

00:04:17.360 --> 00:04:18.480
I'm here for the girls.

00:04:18.520 --> 00:04:21.080
I received a call that you wanted
to return them.

00:04:23.600 --> 00:04:27.680
And also, I did purchase
a Spanish dictionary.

00:04:30.960 --> 00:04:32.120
I didn't like what you said.

00:04:32.200 --> 00:04:33.520
But...

00:04:39.560 --> 00:04:42.040
I will get the girls ready.

00:04:51.520 --> 00:04:53.880
Don't let her take us, Mr Gru!

00:04:55.080 --> 00:04:56.880
Tell her you wanna keep us.

00:04:56.960 --> 00:04:58.880
All right, girls.
Come on, let's go.

00:04:58.960 --> 00:05:01.360
Goodbye, Mr Gru.
Thanks for everything.

00:05:16.800 --> 00:05:18.800
I did it for your own good.

00:05:19.160 --> 00:05:22.120
Come on, let's go get that moon.

00:05:23.880 --> 00:05:24.880
Right.

